# 🧠 Brain Dump

Dump messy thoughts into a chat box and get them back as organised **tasks, notes and ideas**, grouped by topic. An LLM extracts and classifies the items, checks them against what you already have (duplicates, updates, completions), and asks you to confirm before anything is saved.

> **Status:** early MVP / work in progress. 

## Features

- Free-text brain dump → structured items (task / note / idea) with topics
- Prompt-injection guard on incoming messages
- Semantic retrieval (ChromaDB + OpenAI embeddings) to detect duplicates and updates to existing items
- Confirm / edit / reject flow for each proposed item
- Editable topic list
- Eval harness to compare prompt versions and models on accuracy, latency and cost

## Project structure

```
backend/    FastAPI app: API routes, services, SQLite repos, LLM calls, versioned prompts
frontend/   Streamlit UI (brain dump, tasks, notes, ideas pages)
evals/      Eval runner, test cases and saved reports
```

## Tech stack

Python · FastAPI · Streamlit · SQLite · ChromaDB · OpenAI API

## Getting started

**Prerequisites:** [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) and an OpenAI API key.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/<repo-name>.git
cd <repo-name>

uv sync                          # creates .venv and installs dependencies
cp .env.example .env             # then add your OPENAI_API_KEY
```

Run the backend (terminal 1):

```bash
uv run uvicorn backend.main:app --reload
```

Run the frontend (terminal 2):

```bash
uv run python -m streamlit run frontend/app.py
```

The API runs on http://localhost:8000 (docs at `/docs`) and the UI on http://localhost:8501.

## Evals

```bash
uv run --env-file .env python -m evals.run                    # all steps
uv run --env-file .env python -m evals.run --step dump -v     # one step, show failures
uv run --env-file .env python -m evals.run --model gpt-4o --json evals/out/gpt4o.json
PROMPT_<STEP>=<prompt_file> uv run --env-file .env python -m evals.run --step <step>
```